  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "The eval that evolves beside a self-evolving agent: its own lineage of metrics, every candidate it tested with the decision and the reason, what it flags with hindsight, and its own integrity. Every series carries synthetic=\"true|false\" from the trace's harness note; a demo never reads as production.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "e0 is the base metrics; one more generation per agent step that taught the eval a metric. An eval that never grows learned nothing from this lineage, which is a finding about the lineage as much as about the eval.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": ""
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "agentdiff_coevolution_eval_generations",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{family}}",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "How many generations has the eval grown?",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Every candidate is a ledger row, adopted or rejected; the rejected ones and their reasons are in the table below. The eval tests many and keeps few because every candidate must clear a Bonferroni-adjusted level over the candidates tested at its step.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": ""
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 2,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "agentdiff_coevolution_candidates",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{decision}}",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "How many candidates did it test, and keep?",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "1 when both recommend the same generation, 0 when the evolved eval passes over a generation the base would keep because a learned, outcome-linked metric flags its incoming step.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [
            {
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "color": "orange",
                  "text": "disagree"
                },
                "1": {
                  "color": "green",
                  "text": "agree"
                }
              },
              "type": "value"
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": ""
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 3,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "agentdiff_coevolution_recommended_agree",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "base {{base}} · evolved {{evolved}}",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Do the base eval and the evolved eval keep the same generation?",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "The engine's runs advisory: runs at the thinnest task, and its tier as the name. Amber below the 8-run floor for structured tool-use tasks; open-ended reasoning wants 32+. Below the floor every interval on this page is wide by construction: read an overlap as 'these runs do not separate them', never as 'they are equal'.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 8
              },
              {
                "color": "dark-green",
                "value": 32
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": ""
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 4,
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "showPercentChange": false,
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "wideLayout": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "agentdiff_runs_per_task_min",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{level}}",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "title": "How many runs per task stand behind every number here?",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "Computed with hindsight: a learned metric is shown on the generations before it was adopted too, which is how the eval says what it would have seen. The interval is a stratified bootstrap over the runs recorded (resampled within each task), not a population claim.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            },
            "filterable": true,
            "inspect": false
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "footer": {
          "countRows": false,
          "fields": "",
          "reducer": [
            "sum"
          ],
          "show": false
        },
        "showHeader": true,
        "sortBy": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "agentdiff_coevolution_metric",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "agentdiff_coevolution_metric_lo",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "agentdiff_coevolution_metric_hi",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": false,
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "What does every metric say on every generation, with its interval?",
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "labelsToFields",
          "options": {
            "mode": "columns"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "merge",
          "options": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "sortBy",
          "options": {
            "fields": {},
            "sort": [
              {
                "desc": false,
                "field": "metric"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "family": true,
              "synthetic": true
            },
            "includeByName": {},
            "indexByName": {},
            "renameByName": {
              "Value #A": "value",
              "Value #B": "lo",
              "Value #C": "hi"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "type": "table"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "description": "A metric whose change across an agent step has an interval excluding zero in its bad direction. learned=true is a metric the eval learned; learned=false is a base metric whose interval the base verdict does not read. The interval is a stratified bootstrap over the runs recorded (resampled within each task), not a population claim.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            },
            "filterable": true,
            "inspect": false
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "id": 6,
      "options": {
        "cellHeight": "sm",
        "footer": {
          "countRows": false,
          "fields": "",
          "reducer": [
            "sum"
          ],
          "show": false
